-- title:
--   Base change for the edge chart ring Aₑ
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $\pi$ an element of $R$, $q$ a natural number, and $S$ a commutative $R$-algebra; write $A_e(R,\pi,q)$ for `chartERing R π q`, the localisation away from the element `edgeQuot.discr R π q` of the quotient $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}(\mathrm{Fin}\,2, R)/(\,\mathrm{edgeRel}\,R\,\pi\,)$ of the polynomial ring in two variables over $R$ by the principal ideal generated by `edgeRel R π`, and correspondingly $A_e(S,\pi_S,q)$ for the image $\pi_S$ of $\pi$ in $S$. The assertion is that there is a ring homomorphism $\varphi : A_e(R,\pi,q) \to A_e(S,\pi_S,q)$ such that: the structure map $R \to A_e(R,\pi,q)$ followed by $\varphi$ agrees with $R \to S$ followed by $S \to A_e(S,\pi_S,q)$; $\varphi$ sends the distinguished elements `chartERing.ξ` and `chartERing.η` of $A_e(R,\pi,q)$ to the corresponding elements of $A_e(S,\pi_S,q)$; the square in `CommRingCat` with $R \to S$ and $R \to A_e(R,\pi,q)$ as the two maps out of $R$ and $S \to A_e(S,\pi_S,q)$, $\varphi$ as the two maps into $A_e(S,\pi_S,q)$ is a pushout; and $\varphi$ is the only ring homomorphism with the first three properties. Thus $A_e(S,\pi_S,q) \cong S \otimes_R A_e(R,\pi,q)$, compatibly with $\xi$ and $\eta$.
--
--   This is the compatibility of the edge chart ring of Drinfeld's formal upper half plane with base change along $R \to S$, the affine ingredient which lets the charts be constructed once over a base and then specialised. It is used in the construction of presentations of the Mumford tower and in the agreement and transition lemmas for the descended quotient maps on the non-ramified charts.
